MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3 positives (red until §6.3): basic inference with transitive propagation and
local discharge; least-fixpoint recursion incl. self-recursion, mutual cycle
with PARTIAL discharge (distinguishes fixpoint from naive union), and a mixed
cycle with one authoritative member; the "throws A, ..." union marker plus
authoritative "throws ()". 2 negatives: public decls never inferred (already
green under M3 checking); polymorphic recursion over exception-relevant type
params rejected (§6.3.4). Note: "..." in decl clauses is currently
parse-rejected (M1 stub) — §6.3 lifts that for declarations while keeping it
banned in functional types.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
